                        "username": "amboar"
                    },
                    "message": "If you don't mind I'd like to defer these suggestions as arithmetic on void pointers issues an error:\n\n```\n../src/dsp/firmware_update.c: In function \u2018decode_pldm_package_header_info_errno\u2019:\n../src/dsp/firmware_update.c:377:22: error: pointer of type \u2018void *\u2019 used in arithmetic [-Werror=pointer-arith]\n  377 |                 data + sizeof(struct pldm_package_header_information);\n      |                      ^\n```\n\nThe impact by not yet making the change is low as the symbols are static. We can change the declaration in a subsequent patch without concern. I just don't want to be fixing semantics that aren't the error values in this patch."
                },
